 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? So exciting. Are you doing everything yet? Invitations, registration? Crackers and few basic treats are good to have out. Do you want something fancy, or just what's in the cupboard? Like the rental van breaking down, or the cake burning. Keep it simple, just a few basics, and anything special can come out just before people arrive. Weddings are stressy enough without worrying about every little detail. She' appreciate the open box of buns and crackers on table too. Keep few basics out, and only bring out the fancy stuff just before people arrive.",
